### infra/bin/infra.ts
**Timestamp:** Just now (latest)
**Change:** Added MCP protocol configuration to agent002
**Details:** 
- Added `protocol: "MCP"` property to agent002 configuration (line 29)
- This configures agent002 to use the MCP (Model Context Protocol) instead of the default HTTP protocol
- Aligns with the protocol validation logic in agent-core-development.ts that handles MCP vs HTTP protocol types
- Agent002 will now be deployed as an MCP-based agent runtime

### infra/lib/agent-core-development.ts
**Timestamp:** Just now (latest)
**Change:** Enhanced protocol validation with explicit error handling in createRuntimeAgent method
**Details:** 
- Improved protocol type selection logic with complete if-else-if chain
- Added explicit else-if branch for HTTP protocol validation
- Added error throwing for unknown protocol types with descriptive message
- Cleaned up whitespace formatting in conditional blocks
- Protocol validation now handles three cases:
  1. MCP protocol (case-insensitive) → sets ProtocolType.MCP
  2. HTTP protocol (case-insensitive) → sets ProtocolType.HTTP
  3. Unknown protocol → throws Error with protocol name
- This provides better error messages and prevents silent failures from unsupported protocol configurations

