### src/openapi/nationalweatherservice.json
**Timestamp:** Just now (latest)
**Change:** Filtered API to only include weather forecast endpoints
**Details:** 
- Reduced from 6398 lines to 1450 lines (77% reduction)
- Kept only 4 essential forecast endpoints:
  - /points/{latitude},{longitude} - Get forecast office and grid for a location
  - /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y}/forecast - Get 12-hour forecast periods
  - /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y}/forecast/hourly - Get hourly forecast
  - /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y} - Get raw gridpoint data
- Removed all non-forecast endpoints: alerts, aviation, stations, offices, radar, products, zones, icons
- Automatically filtered to 29 schemas, 7 parameters, 3 responses
- Updated API title to "weather.gov API - Forecast Only"
- Created backup: nationalweatherservice-full.json

### infra/filter-forecast-only.ts
**Timestamp:** Earlier today
**Change:** Created new OpenAPI filtering utility for forecast-only endpoints
**Details:** 
- Created comprehensive script to filter National Weather Service API to forecast-only endpoints
- Keeps only 4 forecast-related paths: /points/{latitude},{longitude}, /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y}/forecast, /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y}/forecast/hourly, /gridpoints/{wfo}/{x},{y}
- Implements recursive reference collection to identify all used schemas, parameters, responses, and headers
- Recursively traverses schema references to ensure all dependencies are included
- Filters components to only include used schemas, parameters, and necessary responses (Error, Gridpoint12hForecast, GridpointHourlyForecast)
- Updates API metadata: title to "weather.gov API - Forecast Only", description to "Simplified weather.gov API with only forecast endpoints"
- Outputs filtered spec to './src/openapi/nationalweatherservice-forecast-only.json'
- Includes console logging showing count of kept paths, schemas, and parameters
- Total: 114 lines of TypeScript code
- This provides a minimal, focused API spec for weather forecast functionality only

### src/openapi/nationalweatherservice.json
**Timestamp:** Just now (latest)
**Change:** Flattened all anyOf, allOf, and oneOf schema constructs
**Details:** 
- Successfully removed all 40 instances of anyOf, allOf, and oneOf from the OpenAPI specification
- Used automated flattening script (flatten-openapi.ts) to process the entire document
- allOf schemas were merged by combining all properties and required arrays
- oneOf and anyOf schemas were simplified by taking the first option
- Flattened schemas in:
  - components.schemas (all schema definitions)
  - components.parameters (parameter definitions)
  - All path operations (get, post, put, patch, delete, options, head)
  - Nested schema properties within parameters
  - Content-type-specific schemas in request/response bodies
- Created backup file: nationalweatherservice-backup.json
- Verification: grep confirms 0 instances of anyOf/allOf/oneOf remain
- This makes the OpenAPI spec compatible with tools that don't support schema composition

## 2025-10-27 (Monday)

### infra/flatten-openapi.ts
**Timestamp:** Just now (latest)
**Change:** Enhanced flattenSchema function to handle nested schema properties and content types
**Details:** 
- Added flattening for nested schema property (lines 81-84) - common in parameter definitions
- Added flattening for content types (lines 86-95) - handles response/request body schemas
- Iterates through all content types (e.g., application/json, application/xml)
- Recursively flattens schema within each content type definition
- This enhancement ensures parameters with nested schemas and content-type-specific schemas are properly flattened
- Complements existing allOf/oneOf/anyOf flattening and properties/items/additionalProperties handling

### infra/flatten-openapi.ts
**Timestamp:** Earlier today
**Change:** Added comprehensive path-level schema flattening for all OpenAPI operations
**Details:** 
- Added new code block (lines 102-136) to flatten schemas in all path operations
- Iterates through all paths in openApi.paths object
- Flattens path-level parameters (shared across all operations in a path)
- Flattens operation-level schemas for all HTTP methods (get, post, put, patch, delete, options, head)
- For each operation, flattens:
  - Parameters array (query, path, header params)
  - Request body schemas
  - Response schemas for all status codes
- Uses existing flattenSchema() function to recursively process nested schemas
- This ensures all schemas throughout the API spec are flattened, not just components.schemas and components.parameters
- Completes the comprehensive flattening approach for the entire OpenAPI document

### infra/flatten-openapi.ts
