### src/agent004/main.py
**Timestamp:** 2025-10-29 (Wednesday) - Latest
**Change:** Created new NFL Scores MCP Server (agent004) with ESPN Scoreboard API integration
**Details:** 
- Created complete agent004 implementation (94 lines) for NFL game scores
- Initialized FastMCP server with stateless HTTP mode and host="0.0.0.0"
- Configured boto3 session for us-west-2 region
- Implemented _get_bedrock_model() helper function:
  - Uses us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-20250514-v1:0 model
  - Returns BedrockModel instance with session configuration
- Created @mcp.tool getNFLScores(scoreQuery: str) function:
  - Accepts natural language queries like "today's scores", "Cowboys game score", "week 5 scores"
  - Includes comprehensive system prompt (47 lines) with ESPN API instructions:
    - Guides agent to use ESPN NFL Scoreboard API (https://site.api.espn.com/apis/site/v2/sports/football/nfl/scoreboard)
    - Provides query parameter guidance (dates=YYYYMMDD, week=N, seasontype=2)
    - Includes detailed formatting guidelines with emoji indicators (🏈, 📍)
    - Specifies error handling for API failures, empty results, and ambiguous queries
  - Uses BedrockModel.generate() with http_request tool for API calls
  - Returns formatted score information with teams, scores, status, and venue
- Includes __main__ block with BedrockAgentCoreApp wrapper:
  - Wraps FastMCP server in BedrockAgentCoreApp for AgentCore runtime deployment
  - Runs app.run() for containerized execution
- This completes Task 1 from the NFL agent expansion spec
- Agent004 provides real-time and historical NFL game scores via MCP protocol


